@@ -4,6 +4,8 @@ Linked workspaces run the ordinary `gjc` interactive interface with GJC's own mo
 
 This opt-in command currently supports Linux and the audited Codex 0.153.4 binary with SHA-256 `ac4b47187ebafc6131475c0bb895311828f552c003194193f4e22007ad6f5658`. Other binaries fail admission, including a different build with the same version number. Unlinked workspaces retain normal execution. Native integration adds a local connection registry and a small admission block to the existing Codex launcher; A separate metadata-only selector uses the installed native Codex project browser. The audited storage/model executable and model configuration remain unchanged.
 
+The default audited runtime is an independent full package at `~/.local/share/gjc-shared-session/runtimes/codex-0.153.4-ac4b47187ebafc6131475c0bb895311828f552c003194193f4e22007ad6f5658/`. Do not point shared connections at the mutable `codex-project-picker/packages/0.153.4/` installation: even a same-version UI rebuild replaces its binary and correctly fails the exact-hash guard. Preserve the original audited binary and its matching host/resources in this separate directory; changing a connection's binary path to that identical copy does not change its thread, home, journal binding, or history. A new audited runtime requires a separate review rather than automatically trusting an updated hash.
+
 ## Usage
 
 With the local catalogue launcher installed, both commands open the same native project → conversation picker:
